{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now verify:\n1. Public test.\n2. Differential test vs brute force on small random cases (including reversed, negative, duplicated, nested, touching).\n3. Enormous/performance test.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll verify: run the public test, a randomized differential check against the brute-force reference, and an enormous-input performance test."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"[CALL_00138]","name":"shell_command","input":{"command":"python3 test_public.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport random, time\nfrom intervals import covered_length\n\ndef brute(ivs):\n    pts = set()\n    for a, b in ivs:\n        lo, hi = min(a, b), max(a, b)\n        pts.update(range(lo, hi))\n    return len(pts)\n\n# Hand-picked edge cases\ncases = [\n    ([], 0),\n    ([(5, 5)], 0),                      # empty pair\n    ([(4, 1)], 3),                      # reversed\n    ([(-7, -3)], 4),                    # negative\n    ([(1, 4), (1, 4)], 3),              # duplicated\n    ([(1, 10), (3, 5)], 9),             # nested\n    ([(1, 3), (3, 6)], 5),              # touching\n    ([(1, 4), (3, 6)], 5),              # public example\n    ([(0, 10**18)], 10**18),            # enormous single\n    ([(0, 10**18), (10**18, 2*10**18)], 2*10**18),  # enormous touching\n    ([(10**18, 0), (-10**18, 10**18)], 2*10**18),   # reversed + nested huge\n]\nfor ivs, want in cases:\n    got = covered_length(ivs)\n    assert got == want, (ivs, got, want)\n\n# Randomized differential test vs brute force\nrng = random.Random(1234)\nfor trial in range(3000):\n    n = rng.randrange(0, 12)\n    ivs = [tuple(sorted((rng.randrange(-15, 15), rng.randrange(-15, 15))))[::rng.choice((1, 1, -1))]\n           for _ in range(n)]\n    assert covered_length(ivs) == brute(ivs), (ivs, covered_length(ivs), brute(ivs))\n\n# Performance: 200k huge intervals, mix of overlaps/touching/gaps\nrng = random.Random(7)\nbig = [(rng.randrange(-10**18, 10**18), rng.randrange(-10**18, 10**18)) for _ in range(200_000)]\nt0 = time.perf_counter()\nr = covered_length(big)\ndt = time.perf_counter() - t0\nprint(f\"200k huge intervals -> {r} in {dt:.3f}s\")\nassert dt < 2.0\nprint(\"ALL_CHECKS_OK\")\nEOF","description":"Run public test plus differential and performance checks"}}]}}
